From: Bo-Cun Chen <bc-bocun.chen@mediatek.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_ppe: fix typo for enabling MIB cache

Without this patch, the PPE performance might degrade when per-flow
accounting is enabled: the MIB cache enable register write passes
MTK_PPE_MIB_CFG_RD_CLR as its value mask instead of
MTK_PPE_MIB_CACHE_CTL_EN, so the cache is never actually enabled.

Present verbatim in vanilla 6.12 mtk_ppe.c (mtk_ppe_start accounting
block) -- applies to stock OpenWrt, not SDK-specific.

Signed-off-by: Bo-Cun Chen <bc-bocun.chen@mediatek.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
@@ -1109,6 +1109,6 @@ void mtk_ppe_start(struct mtk_ppe *ppe)
 		ppe_m32(ppe, MTK_PPE_MIB_CFG, MTK_PPE_MIB_CFG_RD_CLR,
 			MTK_PPE_MIB_CFG_RD_CLR);
 		ppe_m32(ppe, MTK_PPE_MIB_CACHE_CTL, MTK_PPE_MIB_CACHE_CTL_EN,
-			MTK_PPE_MIB_CFG_RD_CLR);
+			MTK_PPE_MIB_CACHE_CTL_EN);
 	}
 }
